# libgpg-error -- the error and runtime library every other GnuPG component is
# built on. First of six recipes before gpgme, which flatpak takes as a hard
# dependency with no option guard.
#
# WHY THE WHOLE GnuPG CHAIN IS UNAVOIDABLE, recorded once here rather than six
# times: flatpak has dependency('gpgme', version: '>=1.8.0') with no option to
# turn it off, and gpgme does not implement crypto -- it SPAWNS the gpg binary
# and talks to it over libassuan. So packaging gpgme means packaging gnupg,
# which means libgcrypt, libksba, libassuan and npth, all of which sit on this.
# Flathub's repository signatures are GPG, so none of it is optional.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/libgpg-error/libgpg-error-1.55.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=95b178148863f07d45df0cea67e880a79b9ef71f5d230baddc0071128516ef78
SRC_DIR=libgpg-error-1.55

# --disable-languages. THE FEATURE IS ON BY DEFAULT: configure has
#     if test "x$enable_languages" != xno
# so the Common Lisp binding is built and installed unless it is switched off.
# That is a PAYLOAD rather than a build-time cost -- files carried to every
# system that installs this package, for a language nothing here has. Same class
# as an installed-tests option, and the same reason to name it: the build
# succeeds either way and nothing about a green build says what went into the
# tarball.
#
# --disable-doc. configure sets build_doc=yes by default. texinfo IS packaged, so
# this would succeed; it is off to save the time rather than because it would
# fail, which is a different reason and worth distinguishing.
#
# --disable-static, matching every other library recipe here.
#
# NOT PASSED, DELIBERATELY: --enable-install-gpg-error-config. It is OFF by
# default -- configure only sets install_gpg_error_config when the flag is given
# -- and upstream's own comment beside it reads "gpg-error-config command is
# deprecated". The replacement, gpgrt-config, is installed unconditionally and is
# what modern gpgme and libgcrypt look for. Recorded because the obvious reflex
# on a later gpgme configure failure is to switch this on, and it is the wrong
# lever.
#
# NLS is left at its default, which is ENABLED. gettext is packaged so it
# resolves; named here so the outcome is a decision rather than an accident, per
# the same rule as every 'auto' in the meson recipes.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-doc --disable-languages"
